config DRM_CHROME9
	tristate "VIA Chrome9 HD (VX900) experimental render driver"
	depends on DRM && PCI
	select DRM_EXEC
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_GEM_SHMEM_HELPER
	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
	help
	  Experimental clean-room DRM render driver for the VIA VX900 Chrome9 HD
	  graphics function (PCI ID 1106:7122).

	  This initial driver exposes DMA-backed GEM buffer allocation and immutable
	  device discovery. Rendering remains behind explicit bring-up gates; no raw
	  userspace command stream is accepted. Loading it also requires the
	  chrome9_enable=1 module parameter.

	  If M is selected, the module will be called chrome9.
